invariant: INV-36
file: build.zig
catches: test/host-builds.sh
reason: build.zig stops refusing an AES value for a host object, so a Zig
  build of a server with -DAES=extern on an arm64 or x86-64 target
  compiles the host object and drops the value, which make refuses
  (docs/decisions.md 89). test/host-builds.sh asks build.zig for that
  server's lists on this host and requires the refusal.

--- old
    if (config.aes) |aes| {
        std.process.fatal("AES={t} chooses a device object's AES, and TRUST={t} ROLE={t} " ++ builds ++
--- new
    if (config.aes) |aes| if (false) {
        std.process.fatal("AES={t} chooses a device object's AES, and TRUST={t} ROLE={t} " ++ builds ++
